>> title: Ajitama
>> category: Toppings & Pickles
>> tags: japanese, eggs, ramen, topping, make-ahead
>> counters: Ramen Shop, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: ajitama, ajitsuke tamago, ajitsuke-tamago, 味付け玉子, 味玉, ramen egg, marinated soft-boiled egg, soy egg, jammy egg, half an egg
>> pairs-with: shoyu-ramen, shio-ramen
>> servings: 6
>> time: 8 hr 30 min
>> slack: unforgiving — six minutes thirty and there is no going back from seven: the yolk sets, and a set yolk is a different topping
>> step.1: Printed on the menu as "1/2 Egg". The whole recipe is six minutes thirty and an ice bath.
>> step.2: boil the marinade 1 min, then cool it
>> step.3: boil 6 min 30 sec straight from the fridge
>> step.4: ice bath 5 min, peel under water
>> step.5: marinate 8 hr, turning the bag once

Printed on the menu as "1/2 Egg".

Boil @soy sauce{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @mirin{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @sake{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @granulated sugar{1%Tbs}(12 g) and @water{1/2%cup}(120 mL) together ~boil{1%min}, then take it off and let it come down to room temperature.

Lower @eggs{6%large}(300 g; straight from the fridge) into a pan of hard-boiling water and ~boil{6.5%min}, keeping the water moving so the yolks set centred.

Drop @&(~1)eggs{} into ice water and ~cool{5%min}, then crack and peel them under the tap.

Marinate @&(~1)peeled eggs{} in @&(~3)cooled marinade{} in a sealed bag with the air pressed out, in the fridge, ~marinate{8%hr}, turning it once.
